\begin{frame}{Project Abstract \& Problem Statement}
\scriptsize

\begin{block}{Project Abstract}
FoodRescue is a C++ (OOP + DSA) system that connects surplus-food donors with NGOs and manages
redistribution: donor/NGO/volunteer management, priority-based donation selection and matching,
Dijkstra-based route planning, delivery tracking and file-based storage, with a menu-driven
console interface.
\end{block}

\vspace{0.5mm}

\begin{block}{Problem Statement}
Restaurants, hostels, households, and events often generate surplus food that is
still safe to consume, while NGOs and people in need may face shortages. Without
proper coordination, usable food goes to waste. FoodRescue connects donors with
NGOs, prioritizing by expiry, quantity, and distance.
\end{block}

\vspace{0.5mm}

\textbf{\color{GEUBlue}Target Users / Application}

\begin{itemize}\itemsep2pt
    \item Donors (restaurants, hostels, households, events), NGOs / people in need, volunteers
    \item Application environment: local desktop system used by NGO / donor coordinators
    \item Benefit: less food wastage; surplus meals reach people in need
\end{itemize}

\end{frame}

